    <statement><p>Compute and sketch the vector assigned to the points <m>P = (0,-5,2)</m> and
<m>Q = (3,1,0)</m> by the vector field <m>\mathbf{F} =\left\lt xy,z^2,x\right&gt;</m>.</p>
<p><m>\mathbf{F}(P)=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>\mathbf{F}(Q)=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left&lt;0,4,0\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left&lt;3,0,3\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>P=( 0,-5,2 )</m>, we substitute <m>x=0</m>, <m>y=-5</m>, <m>z=2</m> in <m>\mathbf{F} = \left\lt  xy, z^2,x \right&gt;</m>. We get
<me>\mathbf{F} (P)= \left\lt  0 \cdot -5, (2)^2,0 \right&gt; = \left\lt  0,4,0 \right&gt;</me>
Similarly, <m>\mathbf{F} (Q)</m> is obtained by substituting <m>x=3</m>, <m>y=1</m>, <m>z=0</m> in <m>\mathbf{F}</m> . That is,
<me>\mathbf{F} (Q)= \left\lt  3\cdot 1, 0^2,3 \right&gt; = \left\lt 3,0,3 \right&gt;</me>
